Q: SQL Search for Data in Multiple Columns A: <p>If you are using SQL Server then you can write dynamic query to do so. Please try below query:</p>
<pre><code>declare @sql as varchar(max);
select @sql = 'select * from [TableName] where ' 
    + stuff((
            select ' or  [' + [column_name] + '] like ''%AAA%''' 
            from information_schema.columns
            where table_name = 'TableName'
            for xml path('')
    ) 
    , 1, 5, ''
);

exec(@sql);
</code></pre>
<p>This query will return every row in which at least one column contains AAA.</p>

Q: Populating select box depending on above select box selected in codeigniter A: <p>Controller</p>

<pre><code>function get_city(){

    $this-&gt;load-&gt;model('data_model');
    $records = $this-&gt;data_model-&gt;get_cities();
    $city_html = '';
    foreach ($records as $row) {
     $city_html .= '&lt;option value="'. $row['id'] .'"&gt;'. $row['city'] .'&lt;/option&gt;'; 
    }
    echo $city_html;
    exit;

}
</code></pre>
